  "notes": [
    "SDSS J013655.91+242546.0 (J0136+2425): the paper retains a conditional Galactic-unbound candidacy; the GRF speed only slightly exceeds the local escape speed, and the conclusion depends on the adopted dark-matter halo potential (T:p3-b7). Table 1 lists t_evol = 245 Myr (T:p2-b7), whereas the text states 450 Myr (T:p3-b7); this conflicting evolutionary age does not affect the bound/unbound candidacy.",
    "SDSS J013655.91+242546.0: No numerical right ascension, declination, parallax, or bound/unbound probability is reported. The 12.5–18 kpc Galactic radii (T:p3-b7, T:p4-b4) refer to the place of origin, not the present-day galactocentric radius, so no galactocentric_radius was extracted. The abstract's ≈590 km/s (T:p1-b5) is an approximate rounding of the tabulated 587^{+144}_{-89} km/s and was not recorded as a separate result."
